2026-01-15T20:20:34.875377+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|Despite other reviews and the suggestion by listers the the wifi connection worked well during my stay at this flat with four devices connected at once. Perhaps there weren't many other guests attempting to use it at the time. The flat is in a lovely part of the city just blocks away from two metro lines, multiple bus lines, food and shopping. These are the highlights of this listing. The  price of this accommodation is justifiable based on those factors. The room itself is pretty basic and most suitable for short stays or those who don't mind a "no frills" accommodation. Shower seemed to go from cold to hot with no in between. Microwave was available but needed to be moved in order to use it as it wasn't placed near an outlet. The room features an enclosed outdoor space not accessible from the street (about 7 feet by 7 feet). Mattress was particularly uncomfortable as springs poked through pretty much everywhere, and the mattress itself was thin. The bed features a headboard which frequently made noises that sounded like it would collapse. There were some holes in the wall that seems to be due to some kind of fixture being removed from that portion of the room. Oddly the television had been programmed to automatically change to an adult channel some time after 2am. On a better note communicating with the host was easy and convenient and we were able to arrange getting the keys from a lock box rather than the office when our plans changed and we arrived in London late at night.|5|Despite other reviews and the suggestion by listers the the wifi connection worked well during my stay at this flat with four devices connected at once. Perhaps there weren't many other guests attempting to use it at the time. The flat is in a lovely part of the city just blocks away from two metro lines, multiple bus lines, food and shopping. These are the highlights of this listing. The  price of this accommodation is justifiable based on those factors. The room itself is pretty basic and most suitable for short stays or those who don't mind a "no frills" accommodation. Shower seemed to go from cold to hot with no in between. Microwave was available but needed to be moved in order to use it as it wasn't placed near an outlet. The room features an enclosed outdoor space not accessible from the street (about 7 feet by 7 feet). Mattress was particularly uncomfortable as springs poked through pretty much everywhere, and the mattress itself was thin. The bed features a headboard which frequently made noises that sounded like it would collapse. There were some holes in the wall that seems to be due to some kind of fixture being removed from that portion of the room. Oddly the television had been programmed to automatically change to an adult channel some time after 2am. On a better note communicating with the host was easy and convenient and we were able to arrange getting the keys from a lock box rather than the office when our plans changed and we arrived in London late at night.|LATIN|en|The flat is basic and has some issues with amenities, but the price is justifiable based on those factors.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:20:36.046514+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|Wir hatten einen sehr schönen Aufenthalt in der Wohnung. Sie ist sehr gut gelegen. Eine Bushaltestelle zur Innenstadt ist fast direkt vor der Haustür. Die U-Bahn Station Goldhawk Road ist nur 5-8 min. Fußweg entfernt; gleich gegenüber der U-Bahn Station befindet sich ein lokaler Supermarkt, in dem man alles bekommt, was man so braucht (bis 23:00 Uhr geöffnet). Die Küche ist gut ausgestattet, ebenso gibt es 2 große Betten (eines davon im Wohnzimmer als ausziehbares Sofa). Wir konnten unser Gepäck vor dem Check in und nach dem Check out in der Wohnung unterstellen, das hat uns sehr geholfen. Vielen Dank noch einmal an unsere Gastgeber Stephane und Ellie, die sich aufmerksam gekümmert haben.|0|We had a very nice stay in the apartment. It is very well located. A bus stop to the city center is almost right in front of the front door. The Goldhawk Road subway station is only 5-8 minutes away. Just across the station from the subway is a local supermarket where you get everything you need (open until 11:00 p.m.). The kitchen is well equipped, as well as 2 large beds (one of which is in our living room as a removable sofa). We were able to accommodate our luggage in the apartment before check-in and after check-out, which helped us a lot. Thank you once again to our hosts Stephane and Ellie, who took care of us.|LATIN|de|Guest had a very nice stay in the apartment, which is well-located and well-equipped with good amenities.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:20:36.637252+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|I booked this place for my stay in London because of its excellent location. I was first given a room on the 14th floor but due to a broken AC, I was later moved to the 9th floor. Generally speaking, the room was tidy and everything looked good. I did think that the rooms were a bit too dark for my liking and the light control was all over the place. It would also help if the AC control was closer to the bed because when it got too cold, you had to get up and walk into the living room to change the temperature but this is a minor thing. Overall, the staff was very helpful and they even let me check in ahead of the official time so that was nice.|5|I booked this place for my stay in London because of its excellent location. I was first given a room on the 14th floor but due to a broken AC, I was later moved to the 9th floor. Generally speaking, the room was tidy and everything looked good. I did think that the rooms were a bit too dark for my liking and the light control was all over the place. It would also help if the AC control was closer to the bed because when it got too cold, you had to get up and walk into the living room to change the temperature but this is a minor thing. Overall, the staff was very helpful and they even let me check in ahead of the official time so that was nice.|LATIN|en|I booked this place for my stay in London because of its excellent location. I was first given a room on the 14th floor but due to a broken AC, I was later moved to the 9th floor. I did think that the rooms were a bit too dark for my liking and the light control was all over the place.|0.0
