2026-01-15T20:22:16.281996+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|The guys who checked us in were great and they quickly arranged an additional key which was delivered the next morning.<br/>When demonstrating the pull out sofa bed he immediately spotted there were crumbs all over the cushions and vacuumed them up but this just underlined that the £50 cleaning fee didn't reflect the cleaning as several of the dining chairs also had stains and the whole place smelt of people having smoked in there.  Having left the windows open, the next morning when closed the smell was still not great and it became clear that's because the smell was actually embedded in the sofa cushions.<br/>It's not the owners fault that renters ignore the 'no smoking' rule, but if you are paying £50 for cleaning on top of £850 for 3 nights you do expect that the cleaning staff will ensure it's clean and fresh upon arrival.|5|The guys who checked us in were great and they quickly arranged an additional key which was delivered the next morning.<br/>When demonstrating the pull out sofa bed he immediately spotted there were crumbs all over the cushions and vacuumed them up but this just underlined that the £50 cleaning fee didn't reflect the cleaning as several of the dining chairs also had stains and the whole place smelt of people having smoked in there.  Having left the windows open, the next morning when closed the smell was still not great and it became clear that's because the smell was actually embedded in the sofa cushions.<br/>It's not the owners fault that renters ignore the 'no smoking' rule, but if you are paying £50 for cleaning on top of £850 for 3 nights you do expect that the cleaning staff will ensure it's clean and fresh upon arrival.|LATIN|en|The £50 cleaning fee didn't reflect the cleaning as several of the dining chairs also had stains and the whole place smelt of people having smoked in there. It's not the owners fault that renters ignore the 'no smoking' rule.|0.0
