2026-01-15T20:24:37.290116+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|This below-street level accommodation seems best suited for the young, vigorous, budget-minded traveler, who will be grateful for it's comfortable mattresses, intimate garden, fully-functional kitchen, good Wi-Fi, and the fact that there is a lively pub just across the way. The discerning renter will appreciate the fact that the flat is excellently situated for access to transportation: being barely over two blocks to the Overground, perhaps four blocks to the Underground, and with a bus line that runs down Hemingford Road itself. If one sets out for a Caledonian Road station at a brisk clip he/she may be able to reach the center of London in 25 minutes or less via one or the other rail system---a blessing. Being the owner's home, the flat is well-equipped, with hair dryer, iron, umbrellas, etc. The owner thoughtfully leaves transportation schedules on the dining table for those who plan to tour the city. She is also flexible about check-in times. Residents of the neighborhood, when asked for advice or directions, seem always to be kind and helpful.
<br/>
<br/>Just north and west of the flat the neighborhood takes on a sketchy appearance, a bit drab, worn and littered. However, safety, even at night, turned out not to be a concern, and should not dissuade potential renters who utilize Google Earth as an aid in decision-making. One has the impression that neighbors and shopkeepers look out for one another and want to keep the area safe for families and visitors.
<br/> 
