2026-01-15T20:25:35.198350+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|Siamo stati per una settimana nell’appartamento che avevamo tutto per noi come l’host ci aveva riferito. La posizione è comoda per raggiungere la stazione di London Victoria in soli 20 minuti, da cui passano le metro con cui raggiungere qualsiasi zona. Altrimenti sono frequenti anche i pullman, più economici ma a causa del traffico un po’ meno veloci. Il quartiere è tranquillo, e sulla strada dalla stazione all’appartamento ci sono un sacco di villette tipiche del Paese 😍. Ci sono negozi e ristoranti, fast food e caffè, quindi se non si vuole spostarsi verso il centro c’è comunque qualcosa da fare. L’unica pecca è il balcone che piace tanto ai piccioni.. praticamente non l’abbiamo mai usato ma non era indispensabile.|4|We stayed for a week in the apartment that we had everything for us as the host told us. The location is convenient to reach London Victoria Station in just 20 minutes, from which there are subways to reach any area. Otherwise buses are also frequent, cheaper but due to the traffic a little less fast. The neighborhood is quiet, and on the way from the station to the apartment there are a lot of country villas 😍. There are shops and restaurants, fast food and cafes, so if you don't want to move to the center there is still something to do. The only problem is the balcony that so many pigeons like.. we practically never used it but it wasn't indispensable.|LATIN|it|The location is convenient to reach London Victoria Station in just 20 minutes. The neighborhood is quiet, and on the way from the station to the apartment there are a lot of country villas. The only problem is the balcony that so many pigeons like.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:25:35.575676+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|The check in to get the keys is in a grocery store a mile away. They do not tell you this before you rent. It makes checking in and out a pain. They gave us 1 roll of toilet paper for a week then said we must buy after inquiring about more. The place was super hot and the kitchen was very very bare bones stocked. Upon check out I had asked the woman working downstairs if we can leave our bags for an hour while we ride the cable car. She said no problem as long as it was only an hour so we bought tickets. Then when we went to take our luggage another woman said absolutely not so our money on the tickets was wasted as well. This place was a disaster from check in to check out. I’ve stayed in nocarzs all over the world for over 10 years and this was the worst experience I’ve had. I PROMISE you your money will be better spent at the holiday inn express across the street. This place was terrible|1|The check in to get the keys is in a grocery store a mile away. They do not tell you this before you rent. It makes checking in and out a pain. They gave us 1 roll of toilet paper for a week then said we must buy after inquiring about more. The place was super hot and the kitchen was very very bare bones stocked. Upon check out I had asked the woman working downstairs if we can leave our bags for an hour while we ride the cable car. She said no problem as long as it was only an hour so we bought tickets. Then when we went to take our luggage another woman said absolutely not so our money on the tickets was wasted as well. This place was a disaster from check in to check out. I’ve stayed in nocarzs all over the world for over 10 years and this was the worst experience I’ve had. I PROMISE you your money will be better spent at the holiday inn express across the street. This place was terrible|LATIN|en|The place was a disaster from check-in to check-out, with bare bones amenities and poor communication from the host.|0.0
