2026-01-15T20:25:37.854804+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|Our stay was for six nights with an average of 3 guests. Apartment was very spacious, and if someone was watching TV the sound did not leak into either bedroom which was nice. Only the one TV in the living area. Had a working coffee maker, microwave, stove, oven and washer/dryer combo. Wifi was slow, only ~7mbps.<br/>The beds are super firm, and need updating.<br/>Issue with the bathrooms, the showers couldn't be used at the same time. So we would have to run the bathroom sink faucet to get the shower in that bathroom to turn on. Hot water worked once we found instructions that were hidden that said to use the nest to control the water heater. The shared bathroom toilet doesn't flush properly.|5|Our stay was for six nights with an average of 3 guests. Apartment was very spacious, and if someone was watching TV the sound did not leak into either bedroom which was nice. Only the one TV in the living area. Had a working coffee maker, microwave, stove, oven and washer/dryer combo. Wifi was slow, only ~7mbps.<br/>The beds are super firm, and need updating.<br/>Issue with the bathrooms, the showers couldn't be used at the same time. So we would have to run the bathroom sink faucet to get the shower in that bathroom to turn on. Hot water worked once we found instructions that were hidden that said to use the nest to control the water heater. The shared bathroom toilet doesn't flush properly.|LATIN|en|Our stay was for six nights with an average of 3 guests. Apartment was very spacious, and if someone was watching TV the sound did not leak into either bedroom. Only the one TV in the living area. Had a working coffee maker, microwave, stove, oven and washer/dryer combo.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:25:38.244258+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|Nice little place to call home while in London. Tidy, clean and, in a great location with nearby shops and excellent transport links. The train station and bus stops is mere minutes away, with frequent service. To cap it all off Ailsa, is a friendly host and very responsive to any questions you may have. Would definitely stay again should the occasion arise.|5|Nice little place to call home while in London. Tidy, clean and, in a great location with nearby shops and excellent transport links. The train station and bus stops is mere minutes away, with frequent service. To cap it all off Ailsa, is a friendly host and very responsive to any questions you may have. Would definitely stay again should the occasion arise.|LATIN|en|Nice little place to call home while in London. Tidy, clean and, in a great location with nearby shops and excellent transport links.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:25:38.599521+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|We had a fantastic stay at Peter's. The apartment is located right on Brick Lane, perfect if you want to spend your time shopping for vintage clothes and exploring Shoreditch as we did. We were able to walk everywhere and never had to take the tube. Despite being on a lively street, our room was quiet, for it was at the back of the house. It was clean and smelled nice and towels were provided. The apartment has all you need for a comfortable stay, including a large dvd collection. <br/>Peter is a wonderful host, he was so helpful, polite and communication was perfect! We enjoyed having a chat with him and felt very much at home. We also fell in love with Jazz and Jack (Peter's cats). We absolutely recommend staying here!|5|We had a fantastic stay at Peter's. The apartment is located right on Brick Lane, perfect if you want to spend your time shopping for vintage clothes and exploring Shoreditch as we did. We were able to walk everywhere and never had to take the tube. Despite being on a lively street, our room was quiet, for it was at the back of the house. It was clean and smelled nice and towels were provided. The apartment has all you need for a comfortable stay, including a large dvd collection. <br/>Peter is a wonderful host, he was so helpful, polite and communication was perfect! We enjoyed having a chat with him and felt very much at home. We also fell in love with Jazz and Jack (Peter's cats). We absolutely recommend staying here!|LATIN|en|Guest had a fantastic stay at Peter's apartment, praising its location, cleanliness, and helpful host.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:25:39.956793+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|nous sommes restés 3 nuits dans cet appartement. <br/>L'arrivée est simple avec la boîte à clé.<br/>le jour de départ, un rangement vous permet de stocker vos valises si vous ne partez pas de suite, ce qui est bien pratique. <br/>le logement est très bien situé, à proximité du métro, ce qui nous a permi de visiter facilement une bonne partie de Londres. De plus, le marché de Candem, accessible à pieds de l'appartement, est vraiment génial. <br/>La communication avec notre hôte a été parfaite, elle a été très réactive et n'a pas hésité à se déplacer en cas de besoin. <br/>L'appartement était propre et tout est pensé dans le detail (boîte à pharmacie, café, savons...).<br/>Je vous recommande cet appartement.|2|We stayed 3 nights in this apartment. <br/>The arrival is simple with the key box.<br/>on the day of departure, a storage room allows you to store your luggage if you do not leave immediately, which is very convenient. <br/>The apartment is very well located, close to the subway, which allowed us to easily visit a good part of London. Furthermore, the Candem market, which is accessible on foot from the apartment, is really great. <br/>Communication with our host was perfect, she was very responsive and did not hesitate to move in case of need. <br/>The apartment was clean and everything is thought out in the detail (pharmacy box, coffee shop... we know).<br/>I recommend this apartment.|LATIN|fr|We stayed 3 nights in this apartment. The arrival is simple with the key box. A storage room allows you to store your luggage if you do not leave immediately. The apartment was clean and everything is thought out in the detail.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:25:40.337260+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|This is not a dream home... because it's REAL. Everything has a furnishing (finishing geddit?) touch to it, from the dimmable lights to the extra cushions. You literally have everything you need. The Nest function is pretty nifty also - very handy in the fickle English weather hahaha. <br/>Our favourite part is the kitchen - every single thing you could want to cook/bake (yes, bake!) is possible. Spices? Check. Oven? Check. Cleaning supplies? Check check check. And if you need groceries, you'll be spoilt for choice with the multiple supermarkets around, all within a maximum 10 mins walk. Highly recommend the Turkish marts nearby as well for some awesome pawsome treats in there. Lots of vegan options nearby in the Angel/Islington area if anyone's looking! This location is top-notch for travelling into Zone 1 too. <br/>And thank goodness for Marc on checkout day. Without him, who would have known how we'd manage to carry our luggage down the steps. Phew! nocarz PLUS indeed!!|5|This is not a dream home... because it's REAL. Everything has a furnishing (finishing geddit?) touch to it, from the dimmable lights to the extra cushions. You literally have everything you need. The Nest function is pretty nifty also - very handy in the fickle English weather hahaha. <br/>Our favourite part is the kitchen - every single thing you could want to cook/bake (yes, bake!) is possible. Spices? Check. Oven? Check. Cleaning supplies? Check check check. And if you need groceries, you'll be spoilt for choice with the multiple supermarkets around, all within a maximum 10 mins walk. Highly recommend the Turkish marts nearby as well for some awesome pawsome treats in there. Lots of vegan options nearby in the Angel/Islington area if anyone's looking! This location is top-notch for travelling into Zone 1 too. <br/>And thank goodness for Marc on checkout day. Without him, who would have known how we'd manage to carry our luggage down the steps. Phew! nocarz PLUS indeed!!|LATIN|en|This real-life home has everything you need for a comfortable stay in London, including a great kitchen and excellent amenities.|0.0
