2026-01-15T20:25:59.800841+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|My husband and I stayed here with our four year old child. As a young family, I did a lot of research before booking a property as it was important to me that we stay in a clean, safe, and convenient flat. Julia's place was great! Julia went above and beyond with many small touches to make sure our stay was comfortable. 
<br/>
<br/>The flat has been beautifully updated with many fine touches. The location felt very safe. Buses and markets were very convenient and we were able to get to most touristy places in London within a 5 minute walk and 10 minute bus ride. Otherwise, the area of Chelsea was wonderful on its own with lots of small shops and restaurants. Julia and her husband were very friendly, warm, and extremely helpful during our stay.
<br/>
<br/>The only thing to note is that the room can get a bit hot/stuffy. There is only one window/door combo that serves as the only source of fresh air. In the evenings, when the door is closed for quiet and privacy, the fresh air source is also gone. With three of us in the room (two adults and a small child), it maybe was a bit too much. My husband and child both like sleeping when it's a bit cooler. Probably would not be an issue for one or two people staying. 
<br/>
<br/>Even so, we would stay here again. Overall a great stay! |5|My husband and I stayed here with our four year old child. As a young family, I did a lot of research before booking a property as it was important to me that we stay in a clean, safe, and convenient flat. Julia's place was great! Julia went above and beyond with many small touches to make sure our stay was comfortable. 
<br/>
<br/>The flat has been beautifully updated with many fine touches. The location felt very safe. Buses and markets were very convenient and we were able to get to most touristy places in London within a 5 minute walk and 10 minute bus ride. Otherwise, the area of Chelsea was wonderful on its own with lots of small shops and restaurants. Julia and her husband were very friendly, warm, and extremely helpful during our stay.
<br/>
<br/>The only thing to note is that the room can get a bit hot/stuffy. There is only one window/door combo that serves as the only source of fresh air. In the evenings, when the door is closed for quiet and privacy, the fresh air source is also gone. With three of us in the room (two adults and a small child), it maybe was a bit too much. My husband and child both like sleeping when it's a bit cooler. Probably would not be an issue for one or two people staying. 
<br/>
<br/>Even so, we would stay here again. Overall a great stay! |LATIN|en|Julia's place was great! Julia went above and beyond with many small touches to make sure our stay was comfortable. The only thing to note is that the room can get a bit hot/stuffy.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:26:00.180284+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|We had a great time at Gail's for two days!! First of all the room was beautiful and neat, with our private bathroom, all new and fresh, and a big terrace full of flowers and herbs Gail and Steve grow, where we sat in the evening and could chat and drink a cup of tea after the busy two days we had in London. The house is in the quite neighbourhood and close to several bus stops that get you very fast to wherever you want in London. In the mornings we got a bonus with a perfect breakfast of fruits and yoghurt, cereals and whatever else you could imagine, the best coffee in London (I might add) and the bonus was their little five year old girl Poppy that was an absolute delight and all two mornings that we stayed there we were late going out because she was entertaining us the whole breakfast time before she left for school. Alltogether we would definetly recomend staying at Gail's because she was also very helpful regarding the information about London and things to do and how to get around.<br/>As soon as we come back we will most certanly look to stay at their place again.|5|We had a great time at Gail's for two days!! First of all the room was beautiful and neat, with our private bathroom, all new and fresh, and a big terrace full of flowers and herbs Gail and Steve grow, where we sat in the evening and could chat and drink a cup of tea after the busy two days we had in London. The house is in the quite neighbourhood and close to several bus stops that get you very fast to wherever you want in London. In the mornings we got a bonus with a perfect breakfast of fruits and yoghurt, cereals and whatever else you could imagine, the best coffee in London (I might add) and the bonus was their little five year old girl Poppy that was an absolute delight and all two mornings that we stayed there we were late going out because she was entertaining us the whole breakfast time before she left for school. Alltogether we would definetly recomend staying at Gail's because she was also very helpful regarding the information about London and things to do and how to get around.<br/>As soon as we come back we will most certanly look to stay at their place again.|LATIN|en|Guest had a great time at Gail's place, praising its cleanliness, private bathroom, terrace, and helpful host.|0.0
