2026-01-15T20:26:08.912622+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|We stayed for a little bit more than one week in Edouards Apartment. It‘s located very central and you have quick access to buses or metros to go the city centre and all the main attractions. Also there is a tesco and several little shops nearby if you plan to cook sometimes for yourself, what you absolutly can because the kitchen has everything you need. The apartment itself is cozy, clean and makes you feel at home. Edouard answers very quick and is always friendly and helpful. One of the best nocarz‘s I‘ve ever stayed in. Def. recommend!|5|We stayed for a little bit more than one week in Edouards Apartment. It‘s located very central and you have quick access to buses or metros to go the city centre and all the main attractions. Also there is a tesco and several little shops nearby if you plan to cook sometimes for yourself, what you absolutly can because the kitchen has everything you need. The apartment itself is cozy, clean and makes you feel at home. Edouard answers very quick and is always friendly and helpful. One of the best nocarz‘s I‘ve ever stayed in. Def. recommend!|LATIN|en|We stayed for a little bit more than one week in Edouards Apartment. It’s located very central and you have quick access to buses or metros. The apartment itself is cozy, clean and makes you feel at home.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:26:09.432298+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|Sarah has been very accommodating and hospitable throughout my stay! She’s always responded to my messages. The studio is in the back of the house, about 25-30 minutes to Victoria Station (city center in London) by taking Southeastern Line from Shortlands to Victoria, one week pass ~£55, and it runs until pretty late. The studio itself has a bed, a kitchenette, a washer, a cabinet/dresser, a working TV? and a standing shower. About 10-15 square meters. There’s a backyard which Sarah let me hang out. Anyways, it’s a good studio considering the price. Thank you Sarah :)|5|Sarah has been very accommodating and hospitable throughout my stay! She’s always responded to my messages. The studio is in the back of the house, about 25-30 minutes to Victoria Station (city center in London) by taking Southeastern Line from Shortlands to Victoria, one week pass ~£55, and it runs until pretty late. The studio itself has a bed, a kitchenette, a washer, a cabinet/dresser, a working TV? and a standing shower. About 10-15 square meters. There’s a backyard which Sarah let me hang out. Anyways, it’s a good studio considering the price. Thank you Sarah :)|LATIN|en|Sarah has been very accommodating and hospitable throughout my stay! She’s always responded to my messages. The studio is in the back of the house, about 25-30 minutes to Victoria Station (city center in London) by taking Southeastern Line from Shortlands to Victoria.|0.0
