2026-01-15T20:26:17.057417+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|Not worth the money.  While the apartment was clean and in the heart of Soho-the cost simply does not live up to the value.  I had dear friends fly in from Germany and we were looking forward to sitting together, dining in the apartment.  There was a heat wave that week and the apartment did not have adequate ventilation.  33 degrees Celcius/90 degrees farenheit in the apartment almost the whole time.  All  but one window in a back bedroom was cemented shut, so we could not open the windows to cool down at night.  The living spaces were unbearable.  One of us got a heat rash and none of us slept.  Even though I called and asked for more/better fans, Mike texted that it was too late the first night; then never tried to rectify the situation.  We were miserable.  The apartment did not include air conditioning, but that doesn't mean 33/90 degrees is acceptable. Candidly, while the weather was out of his control, he could have reduced our bill (we could not possibly sit and chat in that stifling kitchen, and eating there was impossible), or found some way to make the stay palatable.  On top of this, the over $120 cleaning fee was adding insult to injury.  We couldn't sit there long enough to mess up the place!  There are equally nice places just outside of Soho, we found for next time that are a fraction of the cost.  <br/>He was nice during the texts, but nice neded action.  He could have taken more responsibility to his guests.|4|Not worth the money.  While the apartment was clean and in the heart of Soho-the cost simply does not live up to the value.  I had dear friends fly in from Germany and we were looking forward to sitting together, dining in the apartment.  There was a heat wave that week and the apartment did not have adequate ventilation.  33 degrees Celcius/90 degrees farenheit in the apartment almost the whole time.  All  but one window in a back bedroom was cemented shut, so we could not open the windows to cool down at night.  The living spaces were unbearable.  One of us got a heat rash and none of us slept.  Even though I called and asked for more/better fans, Mike texted that it was too late the first night; then never tried to rectify the situation.  We were miserable.  The apartment did not include air conditioning, but that doesn't mean 33/90 degrees is acceptable. Candidly, while the weather was out of his control, he could have reduced our bill (we could not possibly sit and chat in that stifling kitchen, and eating there was impossible), or found some way to make the stay palatable.  On top of this, the over $120 cleaning fee was adding insult to injury.  We couldn't sit there long enough to mess up the place!  There are equally nice places just outside of Soho, we found for next time that are a fraction of the cost.  <br/>He was nice during the texts, but nice neded action.  He could have taken more responsibility to his guests.|LATIN|en|Not worth the money. While the apartment was clean and in the heart of Soho-the cost simply does not live up to the value. 33 degrees Celcius/90 degrees farenheit in the apartment almost the whole time.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:26:17.544488+0000 INFO [user]:[base]|Great location, just a few minutes walk from Victoria train/coach station and Buckingham Palace. Walked to Churchill War Rooms and to the Hayward Gallery on the Southbank via Parliament and straightforward direct bus journey to the trendy Spitalfields market and hipster Shoreditch. Really central location. <br/>Nice size living room with decent tv. Great little kitchen, spacious bedrooms. Some carpets are a bit tired and could do with some tlc but all was clean and it didn’t detract from a great stay. <br/>Excellent communication from Dmitry and he was very understanding when our arrival was delayed. <br/>Highly recommend.|5|Great location, just a few minutes walk from Victoria train/coach station and Buckingham Palace. Walked to Churchill War Rooms and to the Hayward Gallery on the Southbank via Parliament and straightforward direct bus journey to the trendy Spitalfields market and hipster Shoreditch. Really central location. <br/>Nice size living room with decent tv. Great little kitchen, spacious bedrooms. Some carpets are a bit tired and could do with some tlc but all was clean and it didn’t detract from a great stay. <br/>Excellent communication from Dmitry and he was very understanding when our arrival was delayed. <br/>Highly recommend.|LATIN|en|Great location, just a few minutes walk from Victoria train/coach station and Buckingham Palace. Walked to Churchill War Rooms and to the Hayward Gallery on the Southbank via Parliament. Direct bus journey to trendy Spitalfields market and hipster Shoreditch.|0.0
2026-01-15T20:26:17.914305+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|I stayed for a week in Shawn's downstairs-upstairs flat and always felt good coming back to it after exploring London. Two tube stations on different lines are nearby, busstop in front of the house, big Tesco around the corner, smaller shops and restaurants along the road, perfect. The road is very loud, no doubt, but I didn't mind although I kept the window tilted. In the summer heat the room (ground floor) was not to warm thankfully. The kitchen has what you need, the bathroom/ separate toilet upstairs as well (hairdryer is in the bedroom in the nightstand, saw that too late, but brought my own anyway). A second room is rented out as well, but I never had problems with the other guest. Shawn is a nice lady near retirement, she wasn't there all the time, so should you have lots of questions or need her help I guess phoning her would have been okay. I think, the price for the room was absolutely fine. Thank you, Shawn, for letting me stay.|5|I stayed for a week in Shawn's downstairs-upstairs flat and always felt good coming back to it after exploring London. Two tube stations on different lines are nearby, busstop in front of the house, big Tesco around the corner, smaller shops and restaurants along the road, perfect. The road is very loud, no doubt, but I didn't mind although I kept the window tilted. In the summer heat the room (ground floor) was not to warm thankfully. The kitchen has what you need, the bathroom/ separate toilet upstairs as well (hairdryer is in the bedroom in the nightstand, saw that too late, but brought my own anyway). A second room is rented out as well, but I never had problems with the other guest. Shawn is a nice lady near retirement, she wasn't there all the time, so should you have lots of questions or need her help I guess phoning her would have been okay. I think, the price for the room was absolutely fine. Thank you, Shawn, for letting me stay.|LATIN|en|Guest had a great stay in Shawn's downstairs-upstairs flat, feeling good coming back to it after exploring London.|0.0
