2026-01-15T20:26:59.426950+0000 INFO [user]:[complex]|I loved staying in James and Akbar's home. I was traveling by myself and this place felt like a home away from home. From the start, communication was great. They checked with me prior to my arrival to confirm my time and Akbar was there to greet me and show me the house. Now, for the house... IT IS BEAUTIFUL! Everything is very tasteful and clean, and the views! Two of the four walls in the kitchen are huge windows from were you can see part of the London skyline (the Shard and the BT tower). I spent many moments looking at this view. I was lucky that my room also had part of this gorgeous view, alongside a very comfy bed, a spacious closet and several extra amenities like a tv, a hair dryer, and convertible power plugs (very useful!). <br/>This place was great because it allowed me to explore the city, basically you can get ANYWHERE from here. It is a five minutes walk to Euston Station, which has the Northern and Victoria lines, and many buses to connect you with the rest of the tube system, as well as railway services to other parts of England. In addition there are so many walking distance places you can visit! I went to King's Cross (~10 minutes), Gordon Square, if you are interested in seeing where Virginia Wolf and other writers from the Bloomsbury Group  lived (~5 minutes), The British Museum (~12 minutes), Regent's Park (~25 minutes), and I am sure many more I did not have time to explore! <br/>James and Akbar also allowed me to use the kitchen which was great because I was able to visit a nearby, and very well stocked Waitrose supermarket, and buy ingredients to prepare breakfast, lunch, and dinner, something to consider if you are traveling within a budget or want to eat healthy during your trip. I was also able to use the washer and dryer, great because I was traveling around England and not all places have this commodity. <br/>James and Akbar are very accommodating, laid-back, friendly, generous, and warm hosts. If I ever return to London I hope to stay with them and I would highly recommend their home to all my loved ones. You should not let the opportunity to stay with them pass you by! |5|I loved staying in James and Akbar's home. I was traveling by myself and this place felt like a home away from home. From the start, communication was great. They checked with me prior to my arrival to confirm my time and Akbar was there to greet me and show me the house. Now, for the house... IT IS BEAUTIFUL! Everything is very tasteful and clean, and the views! Two of the four walls in the kitchen are huge windows from were you can see part of the London skyline (the Shard and the BT tower). I spent many moments looking at this view. I was lucky that my room also had part of this gorgeous view, alongside a very comfy bed, a spacious closet and several extra amenities like a tv, a hair dryer, and convertible power plugs (very useful!). <br/>This place was great because it allowed me to explore the city, basically you can get ANYWHERE from here. It is a five minutes walk to Euston Station, which has the Northern and Victoria lines, and many buses to connect you with the rest of the tube system, as well as railway services to other parts of England. In addition there are so many walking distance places you can visit! I went to King's Cross (~10 minutes), Gordon Square, if you are interested in seeing where Virginia Wolf and other writers from the Bloomsbury Group  lived (~5 minutes), The British Museum (~12 minutes), Regent's Park (~25 minutes), and I am sure many more I did not have time to explore! <br/>James and Akbar also allowed me to use the kitchen which was great because I was able to visit a nearby, and very well stocked Waitrose supermarket, and buy ingredients to prepare breakfast, lunch, and dinner, something to consider if you are traveling within a budget or want to eat healthy during your trip. I was also able to use the washer and dryer, great because I was traveling around England and not all places have this commodity. <br/>James and Akbar are very accommodating, laid-back, friendly, generous, and warm hosts. If I ever return to London I hope to stay with them and I would highly recommend their home to all my loved ones. You should not let the opportunity to stay with them pass you by! |LATIN|en|Guest loved staying in James and Akbar's home, which was beautiful, tasteful, and well-equipped with great views and accommodating hosts.|0.0
